          "code": "CONSOLIDATEENGAGEMENTS",
          "id": "1775167807453",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775167807454_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Input Data:\n For each item in {{$context.$nodes.LOOPOPPORTUNITIES.$output}}, fetch the value of payload.what.summary.\n\nGOAL:\nConsolidate multiple payload.what.summary into a single unified structure without losing any information.\n\nINSTRUCTIONS:\n- The input contains multiple objects, each with the same \"payload.what.summary\" structure.\n\nMERGING RULES:\n\n1. OVERALL SUMMARY:\n- Generate a single consolidated \"summary\" that synthesizes insights across ALL inputs.\n- Highlight overall trends, risks, opportunities, and engagement patterns.\n\n2. SENTIMENT:\n- Combine all sentiment summaries.\n- Identify the dominant sentiment (positive / neutral / negative).\n- Provide a single concise summary reflecting the overall tone.\n\n3. PRODUCT FOCUS, INDUSTRY FOCUS, SIGNALS:\nEach must contain:\n- \"summary\" → high-level synthesis across all batches\n- \"details\" → MUST include ALL unique factual points from every batch\n\nDETAILS RULES (CRITICAL):\n- Do NOT drop any information.\n- Merge and deduplicate overlapping points.\n- Preserve specific facts (names, numbers, products, signals, stakeholders).\n- If multiple similar points exist, consolidate intelligently without losing meaning.\n\n4. NO DATA LOSS:\n- Every important fact from every batch must appear in the final output (especially in \"details\").\n\n5. NO DUPLICATION:\n- Avoid repeating identical statements.\n- Merge semantically similar content.\n\n6. STRUCTURE:\n- Output ONLY ONE object.\n- Maintain EXACT same schema.\n\n7. STRICT OUTPUT:\n- Output must be valid JSON only.\n- No explanations, no extra text.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\n{\n  \"summary\": \"string\",\n  \"sentiment\": {\n    \"summary\": \"string\"\n  },\n  \"product_focus\": {\n    \"summary\": \"string\",\n    \"details\": \"string\"\n  },\n  \"industry_focus\": {\n    \"summary\": \"string\",\n    \"details\": \"string\"\n  },\n  \"signals\": {\n    \"summary\": \"string\",\n    \"details\": \"string\"\n  }\n}\n\nSTRICT OUTPUT RULES (CRITICAL):\n\n- Output MUST be raw JSON object.\n- DO NOT wrap output in ```json or any markdown.\n- DO NOT return as string.\n- DO NOT escape quotes.\n- DO NOT add backticks.\n- DO NOT add newline escape characters (\\n).\n- Response must start with { and end with } only.\n- If a field has no supporting data, output exactly \"\". Do not generate filler, assumptions, risk statements, status labels, or placeholder phrases of any kind.\n- All keys defined in the output schema are mandatory and must be included even when no data is available; in such cases, use \"\" as the value.\n  Example fallback output when no data exists:\n  {\n  \"summary\": \"\",\n  \"sentiment\": {\n  \"summary\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"product_focus\": {\n  \"summary\": \"\",\n  \"details\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"industry_focus\": {\n  \"summary\": \"\",\n  \"details\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"signals\": {\n  \"summary\": \"\",\n  \"details\": \"\"\n  }\n  }"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
